. 
.         * drop observations where month of childbirth = month of survey
.         drop if event_time == 0
(3 observations deleted)

.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         /*
> We use a simple difference-in-differences setup, where we compare households 
> who had a girl to parents who had a boy before and after giving birth to thei
> r first child. We limit our sample to individuals surveyed within 12 months b
> efore and 12 months after giving birth to the first child because we want to 
> separate the effect of having a daughter from the potential effects of additi
> onal children. Our main identification assumption requires that, in the absen
> ce of the treatment (i.e., having a girl), parents who had daughters and thos
> e who had sons would have shown similar trends in the outcome variable prior 
> to birth. 
>         */
. 
.         reghdfe childcare_diff treat i.post interaction, vce(cluster hid)
(MWFE estimator converged in 1 iterations)

